## Folder numbering convention
Every folder is prefixed with a number showing the logical order of the project:
```
1_frontend/   ← build and run this first (Flutter app)
2_backend/    ← second (FastAPI + YOLO server)
3_database/   ← reference SQL (auto-created by backend on first run)
4_docs/       ← this guide and API reference
```
Inside each folder, files are numbered the same way:
`1_home_screen.dart` (first screen) → `2_report_screen.dart` → etc.

**Python note:** Python can't import modules whose names start with digits.
The backend uses `importlib.import_module(...)` for cross-module imports so
the numbered folder/file names stay visible in your editor but never cause an
import error.

