## 2. Flutter app setup

```bash
cd 1_frontend

# Generate Android/iOS platform folders (safe to run on existing lib/)
flutter create --org com.roadwatch --project-name roadwatch .

# Install packages
flutter pub get
```

Edit `lib/6_utils/1_constants.dart` — set `kBaseUrl`:
- Android emulator: `http://127.0.0.1:8000` (default, maps to localhost)
- Physical phone on Wi-Fi: `http://YOUR_COMPUTER_LAN_IP:8000`

Run:
```bash
flutter run
```

---

## 3. Firebase setup (push notifications)

1. Create a project at console.firebase.google.com
2. Add an Android app (package name: `com.roadwatch`)
3. Download `google-services.json` → place in `1_frontend/android/app/`
4. Project Settings → Service Accounts → Generate new private key
   → save as `2_backend/firebase-service-account.json`
5. Run `flutterfire configure` inside `1_frontend/` to auto-generate
   `lib/firebase_options.dart`

If you skip Firebase, everything else still works — notifications just no-op silently.

